==French==

===Etymology===
From {{term|icelui|lang=fr}}, from {{compound|ici|t1=here|lui|t2=him|lang=fr}} or from {{etyl|VL.|fr}} {{recons|eccillui|lang=VL.|sc=Latn}}, a compound of {{term|ecce|lang=la}} + {{recons|illūi|lang=VL.|sc=Latn}}, itself a Vulgar Latin form of {{term|illi|illī|lang=la}}, dative singular of {{term|ille|lang=la}} under the influence of {{term|cui|lang=la}}. (see {{term|lui|lang=fr}}). Compare Italian {{term|colui|lang=it}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-celui.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|/səlɥi/|lang=fr}}, {{X-SAMPA|/s@lHi/}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|fr|pronoun|demonstrative||plural|ceux|feminine|celle|plural|celles}}

# [[the one]]
#: '''''Celui''' qui est là, c'est moi.'' The one who is there, it's me.

